# Original source: ../../../source/public-domain-recipes/kvass/kvass.md
# Retrieved 2026-10-07; upstream commit da84378b36bd5b2e3cb35f610d64630bf1bd899d.
# Source Prep time: ~30 min
# Source Fermentation time: ~1 week
# Conversion note: Source predicts 1.0%-2.5% alcohol and calls for sealed fermentation without pressure-management detail. Alcohol prediction and sealed-vessel handling require review; no invented pressure schedule.

::ingredients

(raisins) 100g
(sugar) 100g
(black bread, such as pumpernickel or rye) 3 slices
(lemon) 1-2
(active dry yeast) 1 package / 7g
(coffee beans, optional) a handful
(non-citrus fruit, optional, such as plums or apples or kiwi) as needed
(water) 1l

::equipment

(pot)
(toaster) -OR- (oven)
(strainer)
(container, sterilized)
(mason jar, sterile)

::instructions

(water) <bring to boil, pot>
(black bread) <toast, toaster or oven, thoroughly scorched to blackness outside>
(water) <remove from heat>
    + (black bread) + (raisins) a handful + (lemon) a few slices + (coffee beans, if using) <add>
    <cool, room temperature>
    <strain, remove all solids, into separate sterilized container>
    + (sugar) + (active dry yeast) <stir, until sugar dissolved>
    + (raisins) rest of + (non-citrus fruit, if using) <add>
    <pour, sterile mason jar if not already in one>
(jar) <seal, lid> <ferment, warm place, 26-30°C / 79-86°F, 1 week or until bubbling stops>
(raisins) + (non-citrus fruit, if using) <remove, from jar>
(lemon) <squeeze, juice into mixture>
<serve, immediately or refrigerate first>

::story

Kvass is a Slavic fermented beverage which is both simple to make and rich in flavour.

